  "question": {
    "text": "One solid sphere A and another hollow sphere B are of same mass and same outer radii. Their moment of inertia about their diameters are respectively $\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{A}}$ and $\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}}$ such that",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0Faat",
      "text": "\n$I_A=I_B$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "O01Gu",
      "text": "\n$I_A>I_B$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qxSa6",
      "text": "\n$I_A < I_B$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "aNlQS",
      "text": "\nyes, $45^{\\circ}$\n$I_A / I_B=d_A / d_B$\nWhere $d_A$ and $d_B$ are their densities.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Moment of inertia of a uniform density solid sphere, $A=\\frac{2}{5} M R^2$\nSince $M$ and $R$ are same, $I_A < I_B$.",
    "image": null
  },
